  14184:  Start an isolated ephemeral Vault server from the declared image, preferably dev mode over HTTP for baseline KV/config-data coverage. Dynamically map its port, wait for readiness, provision deterministic KV data, configure spring.application.name, spring.config.import=vault://, spring.cloud.vault.uri, spring.cloud.vault.scheme=http, spring.cloud.vault.authentication, and the test-only authentication value, then always stop and remove the server. Exercise default/contextual paths, profiles, optional imports, and fail-fast behavior. Use a test-local truststore if TLS-specific coverage is attempted.
  14376:  Every Monday the `create-scheduled-release` workflow packages metadata into the next numbered release if it has changed (§AR-create-scheduled-release). The release is deliberately not gated on the periodic `test-all-metadata` sweep: merged metadata is already gated per-PR (§5.3), and the sweep exercises bleeding-edge JDK and native-image configurations whose failures must not stall the release cadence. Numbered releases consider only semantic version tags when computing the previous version tag, so floating snapshot tags such as `SNAPSHOT` cannot affect the permanent release cadence.
